# The Debian source package, and what it produces.
#
# The counterpart of packaging/gtkpass.spec, and the same package: built from
# the same sdist, installing the same files. Source is gtk-pass-ng, the name
# this is distributed under, and the binary package is gtkpass -- exactly as
# the RPM is, and for the reason pyproject.toml gives.
#
# Almost nothing here is written twice. dh_python3 reads the wheel's own
# metadata and turns it into ${python3:Depends}, so PyGObject, python-gnupg and
# secretstorage arrive as python3-gi, python3-gnupg and python3-secretstorage
# without a mapping table to keep. What it cannot know is below: the versions
# of GTK and libadwaita the application needs, which no Python metadata
# expresses, and which tests/test_deb_packaging.py holds to the same floors the
# spec names.
Source: gtk-pass-ng
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ronny Pfannschmidt <opensource@ronnypfannschmidt.de>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               dh-python,
               pybuild-plugin-pyproject,
               python3-all,
               python3-setuptools,
               python3-setuptools-scm,
               desktop-file-utils,
               appstream-util,
               libglib2.0-bin
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/RonnyPfannschmidt/gtk-pass-ng
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gtkpass
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10),
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.4),
         gnupg
# Per backend rather than per application: the Pass backend shells out to
# pass(1) and syncing a store needs git, while a user with only the Direct GPG
# backend configured needs neither.
Recommends: pass, git
Description: GTK4 frontend for password stores
 GTKPass is a GTK4/Libadwaita frontend for password stores on GNOME/Linux, in
 the spirit of qtpass. It is not a password manager of its own: it stores
 nothing and owns no format.
 .
 It presents pluggable backends, one of which reads and writes the standard
 passwordstore layout, so an existing store stays usable from pass(1) and every
 other tool that speaks it.
